r the trailing four quarters, up 72.1% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 298.4%.","Listed on Nasdaq, Nasdaq, it funds itself from operations ($6.5m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 72.1% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $8.6m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820190/000119312526232857/0001193125-26-232857-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-232857"},{"text":"Gross margin of 298.4% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820190/000119312526232857/0001193125-26-232857-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-232857"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $6.5m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820190/000119312526232857/0001193125-26-232857-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-232857"},{"text":"Net cash of $3.7m against total assets of $293.6m - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820190/000119312526232857/0001193125-26-232857-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-232857"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (-40.4% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820190/000119312526232857/0001193125-26-232857-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-232857"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 40.7% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820190/000119312526232857/0001193125-26-232857-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-232857"},{"text":"Gross margin compressed from 353.7% to 298.4% against the same quarter a year earlier. Either input costs are rising or the company is discounting to hold volume.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820190/000119312526232857/0001193125-26-232857-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-232857"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-373.5% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820190/000119312526232857/0001193125-26-232857-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-232857"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $4.3m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820190/000119312526232857/0001193125-26-232857-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-232857"},{"text":"Shareholders' equity is negative (-$249.2m) - liabilities exceed assets on the balance sheet.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820190/000119312526232857/0001193125-26-232857-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-232857"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 19.4% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (51,758,630 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1820190/000119312526297858/0001193125-26-297858-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 290.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":2.9